Owner: unreagent-worker. ensureBridgeModules (cmd/launcher/bridge.go ~140-247) runs a plain npm install; when it fails and no node_modules existed, the bridge is dropped (~233). The reference project's README reports that npm 10 crashes on the UE LLM Toolkit bridge's dev-dependency peers ('Cannot read properties of null (reading edgesOut)') and works around it in its setup script with --omit=dev --legacy-peer-deps. Unverified here: nobody reproduced the npm crash on this machine. First step: reproduce it against Plugin/UELLMToolkit/Resources/mcp-bridge of the toolkit checkout. If it reproduces, decide whether the launcher installs runtime dependencies only (--omit=dev) — a bridge needs no test tools.

Duplicate of k215, which the Windows agent filed with the measured failure (npm 10.9.2, --legacy-peer-deps as the working flag). Work happens on k215.
